{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Tool Safeguards for DevOps AI.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Tool Safeguards for DevOps AI.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"tool safeguards for dev ops ai tool safeguards for dev ops ai","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Tool Safeguards for DevOps AI.md","fileName":"Tool Safeguards for DevOps AI.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Tool Safeguards for DevOps AI","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-27 12:11\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[DevOps AI Governance]]","tags":[],"links":[],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Tool Safeguards for DevOps AI.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Tool Safeguards for DevOps AI.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"tool safeguards for dev ops ai tool safeguards for dev ops ai","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Tool Safeguards for DevOps AI.md","fileName":"Tool Safeguards for DevOps AI.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Tool Safeguards for DevOps AI","heading":"Tool Safeguards for DevOps AI","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Tool safeguards restrict the actions an AI system may request or perform. A DevOps assistant may read pull-request metadata or suggest a workflow, while deployment, merging, policy modification, and secret handling remain unavailable or require separate approval.\n\nEffective safeguards use explicit allowlists, least-privilege tokens, typed arguments, input validation, bounded output, and an application-controlled side-effect path. The model can select among approved capabilities, but code outside the model owns authentication and execution. Restricting the tool surface limits blast radius even when reasoning is wrong.","tags":[],"links":[],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Tool Safeguards for DevOps AI.md::2","so